% A query whose check follows the literal that binds its key streams its
% rows as it derives them.  a has two edges, so a lookup in the check's
% place would derive a twice and the query would have to gather; the check
% derives it once.  exists-gathered.dl answers the same query gathered,
% with the same rows in the same order.  The counters show the answer
% relation holding none of them.

edge(a, b).
edge(a, c).
edge(b, c).
node(a).
node(b).
node(e).

node(X), edge(X, _)?
